You have to find it first.	你得先找到它。
As you lift the pouch from the stump, you feel its contents shifting inside.	你把皮袋從樹樁上拿起時，感覺得到裡頭的東西正在晃動。
You should try getting closer.	你應該試著靠近一點。
A small, pleasant waterfall pours into a crystal clear lake.	一道小巧宜人的瀑布，注入一座清澈見底的湖泊。
A small spring bubbles up from the rocks here and splashes into the lake.	這裡的岩石間湧出一道小泉水，濺入湖中。
This is a peaceful little lake, fed by a nearby waterfall.	這是一座寧靜的小湖泊，由附近的瀑布注入湖水。
Flowing into this peaceful lake is a small waterfall.	一道小瀑布流入這座寧靜的湖泊。
The flowers are very beautiful.	這些花朵十分美麗。
The fish are certainly getting their exercise today.	這些魚今天倒是游得挺起勁的。
There is no fish here to look at!	這裡沒有魚可以看！
You won't be needing any fish on your quest.	你的冒險用不到魚。
You are standing in a clearing.  The view of the forest is most pleasant here.	你站在一片空地上，這裡眺望森林的景色十分宜人。
There is no fairy here.	這裡沒有仙女。
She is your fairy godmother.	她是你的教母。
It is impossible to acquire a fairy godmother.	你不可能得到一位教母。
There is no need to say, or do, anything.	你不需要說什麼，也不需要做什麼。
FAIRY GODMOTHER: "Gentle Sir Graham, I am your fairy godmother."	教母：「親愛的格拉漢爵士，我是你的教母。」
FAIRY GODMOTHER: "Your quest is indeed noble.  What little aid I can offer you is this protective magic spell, effective but a little while."	教母：「你的任務確實崇高。我能給你的些許幫助，就是這道守護魔法，只是效力短暫。」
FAIRY GODMOTHER: "I shall be watching over you, Sir Graham."	教母：「我會在一旁守護著你，格拉漢爵士。」
While you were wandering in the pen, the goat has wandered away.	你在羊圈裡四處閒晃時，山羊已經跑走了。
The goat doesn't see you anymore.	山羊再也看不見你了。
Silly!  Goats can't talk.	傻瓜！山羊不會說話。
Why?  The goat seems to be following you quite nicely.	為什麼？山羊看起來跟得挺乖的。
You wouldn't get very far carrying the goat.  Perhaps you can get him to follow you if you'd like to take him somewhere.	抱著山羊走不了多遠。如果你想帶牠去哪裡，也許可以讓牠跟著你走。
You cannot do that from outside the fence.	你在欄杆外做不到這件事。
What do you want to feed the old goat?	你想餵這隻老山羊吃什麼？
You can try, but be careful.	你可以試試看，但要小心。
Are you kidding? The goat would never let you!	你在開玩笑嗎？山羊絕不會讓你這麼做！
You do not have a carrot.	你身上沒有胡蘿蔔。
You are too far away.	你離得太遠了。
You and all your belongings are invisible. The goat can't see your carrot.	你和你身上所有的東西都是隱形的，山羊看不見你的胡蘿蔔。
Goats love carrots! The old goat quickly devours yours and stops following you.	山羊最愛胡蘿蔔了！老山羊很快就把你的胡蘿蔔吃光，也不再跟著你了。
Goats love carrots! The old goat quickly devours yours.	山羊最愛胡蘿蔔了！老山羊很快就把你的胡蘿蔔吃光了。
The goat is already following you.	山羊已經在跟著你了。
You need to get into the goat pen.	你得先進到羊圈裡。
You need to get a little closer.	你得再靠近一點。
The goat, unable to see either you or the carrot, is not impressed in the slightest by the carrot.	山羊既看不見你，也看不見胡蘿蔔，對這根胡蘿蔔絲毫不感興趣。
The goat must be on the other side of the goat pen.	山羊一定在羊圈的另一頭。
He's already dead, it just wouldn't be the same.	牠已經死透了，再做一次也沒什麼意思。
You can't do that while your invisible.	你隱形的時候沒辦法做這件事。
You don't have everything you need to do that.	你身上東西不齊全，沒辦法做這件事。
Pelting the goat with pebbles would be a slow and painful way to kill him.  If you feel you absolutely must do away with him, use a quicker method.	用鵝卵石砸山羊，是既緩慢又痛苦的殺法。如果你真的非除掉牠不可，用更快的方法吧。
You need to go into the pen to kill the goat.	你得先進到羊圈裡，才能殺這隻山羊。
You should get closer to the goat first.	你應該先靠近山羊一點。
You don't have a good weapon with which to kill the goat.	你身上沒有適合殺死山羊的武器。
Since you are invisible, everything you own is invisible.  The goat cannot see the carrot.	既然你是隱形的，你身上所有的東西也都是隱形的，山羊看不見那根胡蘿蔔。
There is no goat in the immediate area.	附近沒有山羊。
The fence is too high for you to jump over.	欄杆太高了，你跳不過去。
It would be easier to just open the gate.	直接打開閘門會容易得多。
It is high enough to keep the old goat from jumping over it.	這欄杆夠高，老山羊跳不過去。
The goat pen is crudely made of small tree limbs.  At the other end you see a gate.	這座羊圈是用細小的樹枝簡陋搭成的，另一頭有一道閘門。
You are in the small goat pen.	你在這座小羊圈裡。
Someone has built a small goat pen here.	有人在這裡搭了一座小羊圈。
You see a gate at the other end of the goat pen.	你看見羊圈的另一頭有一道閘門。
There must be a gate around here somewhere.	這附近一定有一道閘門。
That would be very much like beating a dead horse, wouldn't it?	那豈不是像鞭打死馬一樣，白費力氣嗎？
A gallant knight such as yourself would never attack an innocent goat.	像你這樣英勇的騎士，絕不會攻擊一隻無辜的山羊。
The old goat shows some interest in the carrot.	這隻老山羊對胡蘿蔔顯得有些興趣。
Very clever!  You tempt the goat with the carrot and he begins to follow you around.  You've made a friend!	真聰明！你用胡蘿蔔引誘山羊，牠開始跟著你到處走。你交到一個朋友了！
Oh, no!  The goat has escaped through the gate that you left open behind you.  He could have wandered anywhere by now.	糟了！山羊從你沒關上的閘門逃走了，現在牠可能跑到任何地方去了。
There is a small bush near the pen.	羊圈附近有一叢小灌木。
There are several willowy shade trees around the goat pen.	羊圈四周有幾棵柳枝搖曳的遮蔭樹。
This is the crude wooden fence that encloses the goat and his trough.	這是圍住山羊和牠飼料槽的簡陋木欄杆。
The goat, unable to see either you or the carrot, doesn't react to your offering.	山羊既看不見你，也看不見胡蘿蔔，對你遞出的東西毫無反應。
The goat seems to have left through the gate.	山羊似乎已經從閘門離開了。
The gate to the pen is open.	羊圈的閘門是開著的。
The goat pen is crudely made of small tree limbs. At this end you see a gate.	這座羊圈是用細小的樹枝簡陋搭成的，這一頭有一道閘門。
The gate to the pen is closed.	羊圈的閘門是關著的。
You see the goats trough near the other end of the pen.	你看見羊圈另一頭附近有山羊的飼料槽。
The gate is already open.	閘門已經是開著的了。
There is no need to close the gate, since the goat seems content to follow you.	不需要關上閘門，山羊看起來很樂意跟著你走。
The gate is already closed.	閘門已經是關著的了。
When you tempt the old goat with the carrot, he starts to follow you.	你用胡蘿蔔引誘老山羊，牠便開始跟著你走。
You had better wait for the goat, or he may not follow you.	你最好等等這隻山羊，不然牠可能不會跟上來。
While you are wandering about in the goat's pen, the goat grows tired of standing around waiting for you and decides to go on his separate way.	你在羊圈裡到處閒晃時，山羊等得不耐煩了，便自顧自地走開了。
The vines aren't strong enough to be of any use to you.	這些藤蔓不夠堅韌，對你沒什麼用處。
You have encountered an old stone well in the middle of these woods.	你在這片樹林中央發現一口古老的石井。
They raise their colorful faces to the sun.	它們仰起繽紛的臉龐，迎向陽光。
The deep well dissolves quickly into darkness; you can barely see the glint of rippling water at the bottom.	這口深井很快就隱沒在黑暗之中，你僅能勉強看見井底水波閃爍的微光。
You are not close enough to see into the well.	你離得不夠近，看不進井裡。
You see lush green Daventry grass.	你看見戴凡確王國蒼翠茂密的草地。
The well looks as if it's been here a long time.	這口井看起來已經存在很久了。
You can't quite see the bucket well enough to see if anything's in it.	你看不清楚水桶，無法確定裡頭有沒有東西。
From up here, you can't make out any details of the water below.	從這裡往下看，你沒辦法看清下方水面的細節。
You don't see any water here.	這裡沒有看到水。
All the water is at the bottom of the well.	所有的水都在井底。
Now that you've cut the rope, there's no way for you to get the bucket to the bottom of the well.	既然你已經割斷繩索，就沒辦法把水桶送到井底了。
You already have a bucket full of water.	你已經有一桶裝滿水的水桶了。
The goat refuses to go down the well.	山羊不肯下到井裡去。
The sides of this well are too slippery to climb down.	這口井的井壁太滑，沒辦法爬下去。
Since you've cut the rope there is nothing left to climb down on.	既然你已經割斷繩索，就沒有東西可以讓你爬下去了。
You could seriously injure yourself unless you lower the rope first.	除非你先把繩索放下去，否則你可能會嚴重受傷。
That bucket isn't big enough for you and that big goat!	那個水桶容不下你和那隻大山羊！
You'd look silly sitting in your bucket, since the bucket is no longer attached to the rope.	水桶已經沒繫在繩索上了，你坐在裡頭看起來會很傻。
That would be hard to do from up here.	從這裡很難做到那件事。
You can't jump into it while you're holding it.	你拿著它的時候，沒辦法跳進去。
You jump down the well trying to land near the bucket.	你跳下井裡，試著落在水桶附近。
You attempt to jump in the bucket, but miss.	你想跳進水桶裡，卻沒跳中。
The knots on the rope are too tight to untie.	繩索上的結打得太緊，解不開。
You already have the bucket.	你已經拿到水桶了。
The bucket is floating in the well.	水桶正漂浮在井裡。
The old bucket is securely fastened to a strong rope.	這個舊水桶牢牢繫在一條堅韌的繩索上。
You've already got the bucket!	你已經拿到水桶了！
The bucket is floating.	水桶正漂浮著。
The rope is already at the bottom of the well.	繩索已經在井底了。
The bucket is not here.	這裡沒有水桶。
Unfortunately, the rope is no longer attached to the bucket.	很不巧，繩索已經沒有繫著水桶了。
The old bucket is already at the top of the well.	這個舊水桶已經在井口了。
The rope is already at the top of the well.	繩索已經在井口了。
The bucket will be of the most use to you if you don't let go of it.	你如果不放開水桶，它對你會最有用處。
You have no way to cut the rope.	你沒有辦法割斷繩索。
Unfortunately, the rope is now in pieces in the bottom of the well.	很不巧，繩索現在已經斷成碎片，掉在井底了。
The bucket is floating freely at the bottom of the well.	水桶正自由漂浮在井底。
The rope is still wound up at the top of the well.	繩索仍然纏繞在井口。
You look in the wooden bucket and see water.	你看向木水桶，裡頭有水。
You peer into the wooden bucket but find it empty.	你窺看木水桶，卻發現裡面是空的。
You peer into the bucket but find it empty.	你窺看水桶，卻發現裡面是空的。
Move closer to the well.  You can't see in the bucket from here.	靠近水井一點，你從這裡看不進水桶裡。
There is no bucket in sight.	這裡看不到水桶。
The old bucket holds about a gallon of water.	這個舊水桶大約能裝一加侖的水。
This weathered old bucket has served the kingdom for years and years.  It still holds water as well as it did on the day it was made.	這個飽經風霜的舊水桶已經為王國服務了許多年，至今依然和剛做好那天一樣能裝水。
An old wooden bucket is visible at the top of the well.	井口可以看見一個舊木水桶。
This crank is used to lower and raise the bucket into the well.	這根搖柄是用來把水桶放下井裡或拉上來的。
The rope extends down into the blackness of the well.	繩索一路延伸到井底的黑暗之中。
You've cut the rope; there's none to be seen.	你已經割斷繩索，這裡看不到繩索了。
The rope is wound around the crank, hanging above the well.	繩索纏繞在搖柄上，懸掛在井口上方。
A healthy tangle of vines is coiled around the well.	一叢茂密的藤蔓纏繞著這口井。
After you are in the old bucket, your weight causes it to slowly descend.	你進到舊水桶裡後，你的重量讓水桶緩緩下降。
The old bucket disappears into the darkness.	舊水桶消失在黑暗之中。
The rope disappears into the darkness.	繩索消失在黑暗之中。
